  "overview": "Chile is a geographical oddity. On average, it’s less than 200 kilometres wide, but the length of the country spans the driest dessert and the most glorious glaciers. And then you have the mother of all oddities, the island of Rapa Nui minding its own business in the big Pacific Ocean. ",
